                        "entry_id": "77cdfac5-8463-345f-8f19-454a60cd32c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A politician."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bd8c6d9-5dc9-4f0d-ab78-8a11f89c6cd5",
                                "sense_id": "d9dd5cf3-5ab3-39c5-bc52-d633b03ad1cf",
                                "text": "Journalists and pols were cozier then. President Kennedy sipped 1945 Lafite-Rothschild at the Alsops' Georgetown home, and the Alsops dined at the White House."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "244429ec-371c-4a20-86a7-695a166388b8",
                                "sense_id": "d9dd5cf3-5ab3-39c5-bc52-d633b03ad1cf",
                                "text": "The knights-errant of politics could \"tsk, tsk\" all they wanted, but most experienced pols recognized that patronage was the lifeblood of their profession."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
